{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`src/rebar/_engine_support/resolver.py` re-exports 9 names from `rebar._ids` and adds no\nbehavior; ADR 0111 forbids internal shims. Deleting it looks like a module-path rewrite\nacross 51 consumers, but one property makes the order of that rewrite load-bearing.\n\n**The shim binds copies, not references.** Every line in it is\n`from rebar._ids import <name> as <name>` (`resolver.py:15-41`), so `resolver.X` is a\nmodule-level binding distinct from `_ids.X`. `monkeypatch.setattr` rebinds an attribute\non the module object it is given, and does not propagate to the other module.\n\n5 test sites patch resolver names, and every one of them works today only because the\nproduction code under test reads the SHIM:\n\n- `tests/unit/test_attach_commits.py:409` patches `build_resolver_scan_index`, consumed\n  by `_engine_support/commit_impact.py:265`.\n- `tests/unit/test_close_precheck_duplicate_link_c8fd.py:55-58` and\n  `tests/unit/commands/test_replacement_walker.py:54-55` patch `resolve_ticket_id`.\n- `tests/unit/test_close_duration_instrumentation.py:27` binds the module for the same\n  purpose.\n- `tests/unit/test_completion_sidecar_material_balding.py:228` patches the string\n  `\"rebar._engine_support.resolver.resolve_ticket_dir_name\"`, consumed by\n  `llm/completion_sidecar.py:265`.\n\nRepointing those patches to `rebar._ids` while any production module still imports from\nthe shim makes them **inert**: the stub is installed somewhere nothing reads. The test\nkeeps passing and silently stops exercising its branch, which is indistinguishable from\nsuccess. Repointing production while leaving the patches on the shim fails the same way.\n\nSo production and its patch sites must move in ONE change. This story does that. It does\nnot delete the shim, and does not touch the test modules that merely import from it —\nthose stay working against the retained shim and are handled by the dependent story.\n\n## Census\n\nMeasured on `origin/main` at `50d5a36539d` by an AST pass over `src`, `tests` and\n`scripts` that resolves relative imports and scans `ast.ImportFrom`, `ast.Import`,\n`ast.Attribute` and string constants separately, cross-checked against\n`git grep -lF`. 51 consumers total: 42 use\n`from rebar._engine_support.resolver import <name>` (31 non-test, 11 test), 4 bind the\nsubmodule, 4 use the dotted attribute, 1 names it in a string.\n\nThis story takes the **31 non-test importers** — 30 under `src/` plus\n`scripts/backtest_bugfix_size.py` — and the **5 patch-site test modules**. After it\nlands, no production code reads the shim, so a patch on `rebar._ids` intercepts\neverything.\n\n## Change\n\n1. Rewrite the import in each of the 31 non-test files from\n   `rebar._engine_support.resolver` to `rebar._ids`. Names and call sites are unchanged.\n2. Rewrite the 4 submodule binders to `from rebar import _ids as <same-local-alias>`, so\n   the `monkeypatch.setattr` lines themselves need no edit. In\n   `test_close_duration_instrumentation.py:27` drop `resolver` from the parenthesized\n   `from rebar._engine_support import (commit_impact, descendants, resolver)`; the\n   sibling names stay.\n3. Rewrite the patch-target string at\n   `test_completion_sidecar_material_balding.py:228` to\n   `\"rebar._ids.resolve_ticket_dir_name\"`.\n4. Leave `src/rebar/_engine_support/resolver.py` in place.\n\n## Testing\n\nThe failure mode is a patch that silently stops intercepting, which looks exactly like a\npass. Each of the 5 patches is therefore proven live by mutation rather than by its own\ngreen result: with the patch present the test passes; with that single\n`monkeypatch.setattr` line deleted in a scratch copy, the same test must FAIL. An inert\npatch cannot produce that failure. The 5 modules are also run directly, so a regression\nis attributable here rather than buried in a full-suite run.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] **AC1** `git grep -lF 'rebar._engine_support.resolver' -- src scripts` exits 1 with\n      no output.\n- [ ] **AC2** `git grep -nE 'rebar\\._engine_support(\\.resolver|[^.]*import[^)]*\\bresolver\\b)' -- tests/unit/test_attach_commits.py tests/unit/test_close_precheck_duplicate_link_c8fd.py tests/unit/commands/test_replacement_walker.py tests/unit/test_close_duration_instrumentation.py tests/unit/test_completion_sidecar_material_balding.py`\n      exits 1 with no output. The pattern is a regex, not a fixed string, so it also\n      catches the multi-line parenthesized form in\n      `test_close_duration_instrumentation.py`.\n- [ ] **AC3** `python - <<'EOF'` AST check asserting none of the 5 test modules contains\n      an `ImportFrom` whose resolved module is `rebar._engine_support` with a `resolver`\n      alias, nor one whose module is `rebar._engine_support.resolver`; exits 0. This is\n      the shape-complete form of AC2 and does not depend on line layout.\n- [ ] **AC4** `pytest tests/unit/test_attach_commits.py tests/unit/test_close_precheck_duplicate_link_c8fd.py tests/unit/commands/test_replacement_walker.py tests/unit/test_close_duration_instrumentation.py tests/unit/test_completion_sidecar_material_balding.py -q`\n      exits 0.\n- [ ] **AC5** For each of the 5 patch sites, deleting that one `monkeypatch.setattr` line\n      in a scratch copy makes its test FAIL. All 5 failures are recorded in a ticket\n      comment with the test id and assertion.\n- [ ] **AC6** `test -e src/rebar/_engine_support/resolver.py` exits 0 — the shim is\n      deliberately retained, so this slice is provably independent of its deletion.\n- [ ] **AC7** `ruff check src tests scripts` exits 0 with no output.\n- [ ] **AC8** `make typecheck` exits 0.\n- [ ] **AC9** `git diff --name-only origin/main...HEAD` lists exactly 36 paths: the 31\n      non-test importers and the 5 test modules.\n- [ ] **AC10** `make verify` exits 0.\n\n## Ordering\n\nPrerequisite for `insanitary-divine-moa`, which moves the remaining 15 test consumers\nand deletes the shim. Independent of `censurable-exotic-snake`.\n\n## Out of scope — checked, not merely unexamined\n\n- **The 11 remaining `from ... resolver import` test modules and the 4 dotted-attribute\n  test modules.** They keep working against the retained shim: the shim still re-exports\n  the same objects, and none of them patches anything, so no inertness hazard applies.\n  All 15 move on `insanitary-divine-moa`.\n- **`rebar._ids`.** No signature, behavior, or export change.\n- **The shim's deletion and the 2 doc references to it**, both on\n  `insanitary-divine-moa`.","title":"Move production off the resolver shim with its 5 patch sites"}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793382528850196892,"uuid":"aa129e80-ca42-448c-9a12-8f3d89cf96c9"}